---
import Dev from '../layouts/Dev.astro';
import { websiteAssetStatus } from '../../scripts/website-assets.mjs';
import { recipeHash } from '../../scripts/composition-recipe.mjs';
const { outputs } = await websiteAssetStatus(import.meta.env.SOVRAN_REPO_ROOT);
---
<Dev title="Website artwork">
  <h1>Website artwork</h1>
  <p>Only selected public deliverables from <code>press/website.json</code>. Named phones and scenes also drive the homepage. No automatic poster or mockup batches.</p>
  <p>Generate with <code>node site/scripts/website-assets.mjs</code>. Check without writing with <code>node site/scripts/website-assets.mjs --check</code>.</p>
  <div class="dev-atlas">
    {outputs.map(({ output, recipe, scene, current, blockers }) => <article>
      <h2>{recipe.title}</h2>
      <p><code>{output}</code> / {recipe.width} x {recipe.height} / scene: <code>{scene}</code></p>
      <p>{recipe.phones.map(phone => phone.captureId).join(' + ')}</p>
      <p role="status">{blockers.length ? `Blocked: ${blockers.join('; ')}` : current ? 'Current: recipe, source and output hashes match.' : 'Needs regeneration: recipe, source or output changed.'}</p>
      <p><a href={`/social${recipeHash(recipe)}`}>Preview this recipe in the local composer</a></p>
      {current && <a href={`/${output}`}>View selected website PNG</a>}
    </article>)}
  </div>
  <p>Outdated captures can be explored as explicitly labelled drafts in the composer, but never exported by the website generator. App-source freshness does not verify the native build.</p>
</Dev>
